{title: 501 - 'Tis the Blessed Hour of Prayer}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #501 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 501}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]’Tis the blessed hour [Ebm7]of[Db]prayer, when our hear[Gb]ts lowly bend[Db],
And we gather to [Gb]Je[Db]sus, our [Eb7]Savior and [Ab]Friend;
[Db]If we come to Him [Ebm7]in[Db]faith, His [Gb]protection to [Db]share,
What a [Gb]balm for the [Db]weary! O how sweet to [Ab]be [Db]there!
Blessed [Ab]hour [Ab7]of[Db]prayer, Blessed [Gb]hour of [Db]prayer,
What a [Gb]balm for the [Db]weary! O how sweet to [Ab]be [Db]there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db]What a [Ebm7]balm for [Db]the weary! O [Gb]how sweet [Db]to be there!
[Gb]Blessed hour [Db]of prayer, [Eb7]Blessed hour [Ab]of prayer,
[Db]What a [Ebm7]balm for [Db]the weary! O [Gb]how sweet [Db]to be there!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]'Tis the [Ebm7]blessed hour [Db]of prayer, [Gb]when the [Db]Savior draws near,
[Gb]With a [Db]tender compassion [Eb7]His children [Ab]to hear;
[Db]When He [Ebm7]tells us [Db]we may cast [Gb]at His [Db]feet every care,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]'Tis the [Ebm7]blessed hour [Db]of prayer, [Gb]when the [Db]tempted and tried
[Gb]To the [Db]Savior who [Eb7]loves them [Ab]their sorrows confide;
[Db]With [Ebm7]a sympathizing [Db]heart [Gb]He removes [Db]every care;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]'Tis the [Ebm7]blessed hour [Db]of prayer, [Gb]trusting Him [Db]we believe,
[Gb]That the [Db]blessings we're [Eb7]needing we'll [Ab]surely receive;
[Db]In the [Ebm7]fullness of [Db]this trust [Gb]we shall [Db]lose every care;
{end_of_verse}
